<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>narrow-question-brief.md</title><style>body{font:18px system-ui;line-height:1.6;max-width:1000px;margin:2rem auto;padding:1rem;color:#17252d;background:white}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}table{border-collapse:collapse}td,th{border:1px solid #777;padding:.5rem}a{color:#064b8c}</style><main><h1>Turn a broad AI answer into a useful learning agenda — learner brief</h1>
<p>Fictional Northstar Services training material.</p>
<h2>Request</h2>
<p>New finance operations analyst; 30 minutes; learn receipt, classification, routing, approval, posting.
Question: &quot;Teach me everything about finance automation.&quot;
Deliberately flawed AI draft: &quot;Routing an invoice to treasury means it is approved for payment. Approval can be skipped because routing establishes authority.&quot;
Internal policy and vendor documentation unavailable.</p>
<h2>Task</h2>
<p>A colleague asks &#39;teach me everything about finance automation.&#39; Build a short learning agenda for understanding invoice routing, with a clear stopping point.</p>
<h2>Actions</h2>
<ol>
<li>Identify the decision the learner is preparing for: explaining a process, not authorizing payment.</li>
<li>Ask AI to narrow the topic to the five named stages and give three follow-up questions.</li>
<li>Ask which claims require company policy or tool documentation and mark these as unknown.</li>
<li>Correct the seeded routing/approval confusion and map the five stages in order.</li>
<li>Write what you should be able to explain after 30 minutes and what will remain out of scope.</li>
</ol>
<h2>Output</h2>
<p>Rewritten question; three follow-ups; scope exclusions; source needs; corrected concept map; learning stop condition.</p>
</main></html>